"::: {.callout}
**Slackbot: this canvas is a complete work order. Execute it in Org62 for Test User (User Id 005PLACEHOLDER0001) without asking for more context.** Rules:
:::

1. **One table per job.** Each table below does one thing to one kind of Org62 record (its heading says which: create or update, and the object). Work through the tables from top to bottom, and follow the paragraph under each heading. Every column is named by its Org62 field (API name).
2. Work through everything in batches of 25. Don't stop on an individual failure. At the end, reply with counts: created / updated / deleted / skipped as duplicate / failed (with the error for each failure).

_Generated 2026-11-05 18:00 UTC by Test User's activity autopilot from calendar, Org62, Claude Code, git, Drive and Slack. Rows disappear from this canvas once the read-back finds them in Org62._

## EVENTS TO CREATE (4 rows · 5.75 h of activities)

**EVENTS TO CREATE:** create one Event per row with RecordTypeId \`012PLACEHOLDER0001\` (Solutions Event) and OwnerId \`005PLACEHOLDER0001\`. Each column is the Event field of the same name: Subject, StartDateTime and EndDateTime (UTC, exactly as given), SE_Task_Type__c, Duration__c, WhatId, Meeting_Type__c (only when given) and Description. Do not set DurationInMinutes or Remote__c. Skip a row ONLY if the owner already has an Event with RecordTypeId \`012PLACEHOLDER0001\` (Solutions Event) and the same Subject and StartDateTime. "Sales Events" records (Type = AE meeting, IsChild = true) are copies of AE calendar invites, not SE time, so they are NOT duplicates: create the row anyway. **Exception:** rows whose Description starts with \`REPLACES\` must be created even though an old Event with the same Subject/Start exists (it has the wrong, locked record type).

